            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## What's new in Aretas 0.1.9

*2026-08-07*

Aretas now tells you when an update turns off Messages access, and every waiting decision has a place to be decided.

- If a macOS update switches off Aretas's access to Messages, Aretas now notices and shows you exactly how to turn it back on.
- The things Aretas wasn't sure about can now be decided — fold two records together or keep them separate, one look at a time.
- A new Tasks section shows commitments found in your meetings, each with the exact words that were said, for you to approve or decline.
- Every analysis now shows what it cost right on its row, and unknown costs say so instead of showing a number.
- Money is described the same way on every screen.
- An answer you paid for now survives closing and reopening the app.
]]></description>
