        <item>
            <title>0.1.8</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 09:27:31 -0600</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>13</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.1.8</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## What's new in Aretas 0.1.8

*2026-08-07*

Aretas now waits until it has read everything, shows you what analysis costs, and asks before changing anything.

- Fixed a rare freeze that could lock the app during its first big scan.
- Review now waits until your mail, messages, and calls are fully read before showing results, and says what it is still reading.
- New: ask Claude for a written summary of any correspondence report.
- New: Aretas can notice when something changed about a person — a new job, a new number — and asks you before anything is updated.
- New: help deciding an ambiguous contact detail, one at a time, with the cost shown before you start.
- See what analysis costs as it happens, and set your own spending limit.
- The Review tab now opens on Found — the people Aretas has found for you.
- Screens now say when something could not be read, instead of showing a number that looks certain.
- Reporting a problem now tells you exactly where your report goes.
]]></description>
